  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Civil Society&#xe2;&#x20ac;&#x201c;Led Transformation Toward Gender-Responsive Climate Resilience in Coastal Bangladesh and Vietnam, 2026-2028</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Enhanced participation, decision-making agency and role of grassroots CSOs, women and
youth on gender-responsive climate adaptation and disaster risk reduction to ensure that no one is left behind.
2. CSO-led integrated and nexus approach to climate change and disaster risk management actions for improved community resilience (mitigative, adaptive and transformative capacity)</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to promote the active engagement and contribution of civil society in Bangladesh and Vietnam to the long-term goal of full and meaningful participation of women and youth in strategic and operational decision-making about climate adaptation and disaster risk reduction to ensure actions to prepare, protect and adapt to the consequences of climate change is gender-responsive and based on local knowledge and needs.</narrative>
  </description>
